@startuml Linkwise_Chat_Recovery
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam maxMessageSize 130
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 28
title UML sequence: lost receipt, duplicate retry and restart (proposed)
participant "Sender outbox" as A
participant "Receiver inbox" as B
participant "Receiver agent host" as Agent
A -> B : complete message M + digest D
B -> B : atomic commit M, dedup key,\nreceipt R
B -x A : R lost during link failure
A -> A : restart; recover unresolved\nM; invalidate old grants
A -> A : re-evaluate expiry/policy;\nobtain fresh contact\nauthority
A -> B : retry M with same sender,\nmessage ID and digest
alt same key and same digest
 B -> B : find committed M; do not\nenqueue duplicate
 B --> A : replay existing receipt R
else same key but different digest
 B --> A : reject identity/content\nconflict
end
Agent -> B : poll inbox / resume from\ndurable cursor
B --> Agent : M with processing state
note over B,Agent
One durable inbox entry does not ensure one external
action.
Agent handlers must use idempotency and
transactional checkpoints.
Expired dedup records require a defined replay-
retention policy.
end note
@enduml
